From 1708e96dbe23a694556500072cae8ce49f17c9bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:31:35 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18b: surface Chromium downloads to the host

Observe each bridge profile's DownloadManager with Chromium's AllDownloadItemNotifier and report created, updated, completed, interrupted, cancelled and removed transitions. Each event carries id, GUID, initiating tab, URL, target path, MIME type, received and total bytes, state, danger type and interrupt reason. Pause, resume, cancel, open, reveal and remove call DownloadItem's own methods. ReArcDownloadSetPolicy writes Chromium's DownloadPrefs directory and disables prompting. In embedded mode, ChromeDownloadManagerDelegate opens downloads with the platform handler instead of creating a Chrome window, and never shows its file picker: preference and save-as confirmations continue at the suggested path, all others cancel. The DownloadManager stays the source of truth for history, safety checks, auto-resumption and chrome://downloads.

Advertise downloads in ABI 1.17 / bridge 0.19.0 with additive symbols only and unchanged ABI 1.13/1.14 layouts. Build p53; the new native downloads host covers policy, completion into the directory, pause/resume/cancel/remove, interruption and a picker-free OTR download. All native hosts, G1-G5 and four stress processes / sixteen shutdown tabs pass in gates-tab035.log.

Last rebased: 2026-11-03 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
